{"full":"hf:RiverRider/srt-sunstone","spaceId":"RiverRider/srt-sunstone","name":"Gemma-4-31B-it SRT-Sunstone","source":"huggingface","description":"A read-out that reads images — trained only on words","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","semiotic","cross-modal","interpretability","read-out","gemma-4","representation-learning","vision-language","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":3,"created":"2026-07-03T21:01:22.000Z","updated":"2026-08-28T19:51:27.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://riverrider-srt-sunstone.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/RiverRider/srt-sunstone","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:35.875Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:35.875Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:35.875Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🔮","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SRT Sunstone is a live demonstration that a read-out head trained on text alone can interpret images — with zero image training. It is a 12.3 M side-channel head on a frozen google/gemma-4-31B-it, taught one thing from prose: to tell apart communities of language use. Point it at a picture and it names what the image means and the discourse it evokes.","This is the semiotic claim of the SRT (Semiotic-Reflexive Transformer) program made concrete: the read-out interprets a sign by its place in a shared system of meaning, independent of whether the sign arrived as a word or an image.","Pick any category in the gallery. For each one you see:"],"features":["The words it means — the image, placed in a shared word space, retrieves","The caption it retrieves — the same image state picks a full sentence","The discourse it evokes — the nearest of 35 discourse communities the head"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/RiverRider/srt-sunstone/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c75753fe68284b7efba378e439381647f67ff9d2959909f3126db1a49e9ba473","extractedAt":"2026